powerful, and secure tools

00:31:31.020 --> 00:31:35.280
to help people communicate and
collaborate with one another,

00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:37.950
no matter where they are.

00:31:37.950 --> 00:31:42.180
We introduced Smart Canvas to
help content creators remove

00:31:42.180 --> 00:31:44.940
friction from
workflows and enable

00:31:44.940 --> 00:31:47.880
teams to stay connected
outside of meetings,

00:31:47.880 --> 00:31:52.880
to foster well-being, and
reduce video call fatigue.

00:31:52.880 --> 00:31:55.670
We made communication
and collaboration

00:31:55.670 --> 00:31:57.440
completely seamless.

00:31:57.440 --> 00:32:01.280
For instance, users can
easily present and collaborate

00:32:01.280 --> 00:32:04.760
in meetings, create meeting
notes from their calendar,

00:32:04.760 --> 00:32:08.450
present in Meet directly
from Docs, Sheets, or Slides,

00:32:08.450 --> 00:32:12.140
and collaborate directly
from Chat and Spaces.

00:32:12.140 --> 00:32:16.310
We optimized collaboration
from all mobile devices

00:32:16.310 --> 00:32:21.440
to provide great experiences for
frontline workers who make up

00:32:21.440 --> 00:32:24.620
80% of the global workforce.

00:32:24.620 --> 00:32:28.010
One of America's largest
hospital systems,

00:32:28.010 --> 00:32:31.370
CommonSpirit Health, is
advancing its mission

00:32:31.370 --> 00:32:34.640
during the pandemic by
making its frontline doctors

00:32:34.640 --> 00:32:38.330
and nurses productive
at Google Workspace.

00:32:38.330 --> 00:32:41.060
Since hybrid work has
removed the notion

00:32:41.060 --> 00:32:44.720
of a physical location
for work, Google Workspace

00:32:44.720 --> 00:32:50.420
created spaces, a unified
digital location for work.

00:32:50.420 --> 00:32:55.700
Today, more than 3 billion users
move security and seamlessly

00:32:55.700 --> 00:33:01.190
between Mail, Chat, Audio,
Video, and now Spaces.

00:33:01.190 --> 00:33:07.310
And you too can choose among
the over 5,300 public apps

00:33:07.310 --> 00:33:08.660
in our marketplace.

00:33:08.660 --> 00:33:12.080
And you can also add
thousands of private apps

00:33:12.080 --> 00:33:15.520
to enhance your workspace.

00:33:15.520 --> 00:33:18.190
And I want to step
aside for just a minute

00:33:18.190 --> 00:33:21.920
and tell you about a hidden
secret in our portfolio

00:33:21.920 --> 00:33:26.620
of products, AppSheet,
our notebook platform that

00:33:26.620 --> 00:33:31.510
makes it easy for everyone, not
just professional developers,

00:33:31.510 --> 00:33:34.930
to build amazing
apps and workflows.

00:33:34.930 --> 00:33:39.025
For instance, property managers
at [INAUDIBLE] Properties

00:33:39.025 --> 00:33:41.980
used AppSheet to
build a mobile app,

00:33:41.980 --> 00:33:45.430
to log, track, and resolve
problems with headquarters,

00:33:45.430 --> 00:33:49.370
replacing a multi-step
manual process.

00:33:49.370 --> 00:33:51.670
We're also partnering
with Citrix

00:33:51.670 --> 00:33:55.420
because employees sometimes
need access to Windows,

00:33:55.420 --> 00:33:59.050
and Mac OS applications,
and desktops directly

00:33:59.050 --> 00:34:00.790
served from the Cloud.

00:34:00.790 --> 00:34:02.860
We're expanding our
partnership with Citrix

00:34:02.860 --> 00:34:07.480
today to deliver an integrated
desktop as a service solution

00:34:07.480 --> 00:34:12.100
purpose-built on Google Cloud.

00:34:12.100 --> 00:34:16.989
Now, customers ask us, do we
know that our data, systems,

00:34:16.989 --> 00:34:19.000
and users are secure?

00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:23.600
And how do we keep them
secure in the future?

00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:28.699
As more digital users access
more data from more locations,

00:34:28.699 --> 00:34:33.440
the risk of cybersecurity
breaches is accelerating.

00:34:33.440 --> 00:34:36.739
By pioneering new
approaches to security,

00:34:36.739 --> 00:34:39.710
Google keeps more
people safe online

00:34:39.710 --> 00:34:43.070
than anyone else in the world.

00:34:43.070 --> 00:34:45.080
Take, for instance, JetBlue.

00:34:45.080 --> 00:34:48.409
It's keeping its system
secure, protecting

00:34:48.409 --> 00:34:52.550
the data of all its travelers,
and modernizing its security

00:34:52.550 --> 00:34:56.330
operations using Chronicle
to detect threats

00:34:56.330 --> 00:34:59.810
across petabytes of
security telemetry,

00:34:59.810 --> 00:35:03.500
eliminating data blind spots.

00:35:03.500 --> 00:35:07.160
Commerzbank, one of
Germany's largest banks,

00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:10.460
is using a new certificate
authority service

00:35:10.460 --> 00:35:14.240
to verify machine and
workload identity,

00:35:14.240 --> 00:35:18.740
improving security, simplifying
operations, eliminating

00:35:18.740 --> 00:35:20.960
entire classes of threats.

00:35:20.960 --> 00:35:23.870
Secure by default
drives customers

00:35:23.870 --> 00:35:25.460
to choose Google Cloud.

00:35:25.460 --> 00:35:28.220
First, we've
implemented zero trust

00:35:28.220 --> 00:35:31.250
at the core of our services
and our operations,

00:35:31.250 --> 00:35:34.040
enabling you to trust nothing.

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:38.580
Second, we've built cloud scale
threat detection and response,

00:35:38.580 --> 00:35:41.060
allowing you to
detect everything.

00:35:41.060 --> 00:35:44.570
And third, we know it's
not just about tools.

00:35:44.570 --> 00:35:48.080
We provide the
advisory services you

00:35:48.080 --> 00:35:50.960
need to transform
security operations.

00:35:50.960 --> 00:35:54.860
We keep customers safe with
BeyondCorp Enterprise, which

00:35:54.860 --> 00:35:58.730
enables zero trust
access for all users.

00:35:58.730 --> 00:36:01.790
Today, we're
expanding BeyondCorp

00:36:01.790 --> 00:36:06.050
to all your applications--
modern and legacy, web

00:36:06.050 --> 00:36:10.020
and desktop, and even to
production environments.

00:36:10.020 --> 00:36:14.390
We keep customers safe by
eliminating software supply

00:36:14.390 --> 00:36:16.690
chain vulnerabilities.

00:36:16.690 --> 00:36:20.650
Over the past two decades,
we've pioneered an approach

00:36:20.650 --> 00:36:23.890
to secure our own
software supply chain.

00:36:23.890 --> 00:36:25.870
We are now making
that technology

00:36:25.870 --> 00:36:29.950
available through the
SLSA Open Source Framework

00:36:29.950 --> 00:36:32.440
and as managed
services in our Cloud

00:36:32.440 --> 00:36:37.180
to help you secure your
own software supply chain.

00:36:37.180 --> 00:36:40.570
We keep customers safe by
integrating Chronicle's threat

00:36:40.570 --> 00:36:44.540
detection capability with
our Security Command Center,

00:36:44.540 --> 00:36:48.730
allowing you to respond
faster to potential risks.

00:36:48.730 --> 00:36:54.130
And we keep customers safe by
bringing our security expertise

00:36:54.130 --> 00:36:59.110
to you with our Google
Cybersecurity Action Team,

00:36:59.110 --> 00:37:02.050
a team of our leading
security experts

00:37:02.050 --> 00:37:05.800
who can help shape your
security transformation

00:37:05.800 --> 00:37:08.650
from your very
first implementation

00:37:08.650 --> 00:37:11.740
through responding
to a major incident

00:37:11.740 --> 00:37:16.730
and engineering new
solutions as needs change.

00:37:16.730 --> 00:37:20.710
Finally, we continue to
expand our security ecosystem

00:37:20.710 --> 00:37:24.850
with companies like Fortinet,
Palo Alto Networks, [INAUDIBLE]

00:37:24.850 --> 00:37:26.950
and so many more.

00:37:26.950 --> 00:37:29.650
Today, I'd like to
welcome your new security

00:37:29.650 --> 00:37:34.090
partner, Cybereason, with
whom we are collaborating

00:37:34.090 --> 00:37:37.690
to deliver a new, extended
detection and response

00:37:37.690 --> 00:37:40.420
offering that will
combine Chronicle's

00:37:40.420 --> 00:37:44.350
capability with
Cybereason's MalOps Engine

00:37:44.350 --> 00:37:50.120
for faster, easier threat
detection and response.

00:37:50.120 --> 00:37:54.080
Our products, our new
Cybersecurity Action Team,

00:37:54.080 --> 00:37:58.070
and our partnerships
all make the world safer

00:37:58.070 --> 00:38:00.170
from cyber threats.

00:38:00.170 --> 00:38:04.730
To talk more about how we help
keep each and every one of you

00:38:04.730 --> 00:38:08.030
secure and how we're
addressing some

00:38:08.030 --> 00:38:11.030
of the most important
challenges facing our world,

00:38:11.030 --> 00:38:13.460
I'd like to invite Sundar back.

00:38:13.460 --> 00:38:15.660
Thank you.

00:38:15.660 --> 00:38:18.480
SUNDAR PICHAI:
Thank you, Thomas.

00:38:18.480 --> 00:38:23.400
Security is top of mind for
businesses of all sizes,

00:38:23.400 --> 00:38:25.980
as well as the public sector.

00:38:25.980 --> 00:38:29.580
And despite the progress that
has been made in cybersecurity,

00:38:29.580 --> 00:38:33.750
large scale breaches
continue to make headlines.

00:38:33.750 --> 00:38:36.090
That's why, in August,
Google announced

00:38:36.090 --> 00:38:39.570
we will invest $10 billion
over the next five years

00:38:39.570 --> 00:38:41.940
to strengthen cybersecurity.

00:38:41.940 --> 00:38:44.880
That includes expanding
zero trust programs,

00:38:44.880 --> 00:38:47.580
helping secure the
software supply chain,

00:38:47.580 --> 00:38:50.940
and enhancing open
source security.

00:38:50.940 --> 00:38:53.250
A new challenge is
keeping collaboration

00:38:53.250 --> 00:38:58.140
secure and private, as we move
to hybrid work environments.

00:38:58.140 --> 00:39:02.820
To help, we are introducing
a new Work Safer program.

00:39:02.820 --> 00:39:06.930
It provides the highest level
of security for your email,

00:39:06.930 --> 00:39:11.160
meetings, messaging, and
more, and brings together

00:39:11.160 --> 00:39:15.300
Google Workspace with Titan
Security Keys, BeyondCorp,

00:39:15.300 --> 00:39:19.710
and other secure technologies,
products, and partners.

00:39:19.710 --> 00:39:22.440
Now, every kind of
organization in business

00:39:22.440 --> 00:39:25.140
can access the same
security protections

00:39:25.140 --> 00:39:28.870
that make work safer at Google.

00:39:28.870 --> 00:39:31.740
Security is an issue
that affects us all.

00:39:31.740 --> 00:39:35.880
And this brings us to the
last question Thomas posed.

00:39:35.880 --> 00:39:38.400
Are we addressing the
most important challenges

00:39:38.400 --> 00:39:40.430
facing our world?

00:39:40.430 --> 00:39:43.150
Climate change is one of
the most profound challenges

00:39:43.150 --> 00:39:44.590
we face.

00:39:44.590 --> 00:39:48.460
It'll take all of us working
together to solve it.

00:39:48.460 --> 00:39:51.250
Sustainability has been
a core value for us

00:39:51.250 --> 00:39:53.680
for more than two decades.

00:39:53.680 --> 00:39:56.860
Google has been carbon
neutral since 2007.

00:39:56.860 --> 00:40:00.820
And we've matched our operations
with 100% renewable energy

00:40:00.820 --> 00:40:03.340
over four consecutive years.

00:40:03.340 --> 00:40:06.790
Last year, we set out to make
our third decade of climate

00:40:06.790 --> 00:40:09.400
action our biggest yet.

00:40:09.400 --> 00:40:11.710
That included a bold
commitment to operate

00:40:11.710 --> 00:40:16.210
on 24/7 carbon free energy
across our offices and data

00:40:16.210 --> 00:40:18.800
centers by 2030.

00:40:18.800 --> 00:40:21.110
And last week, we
announced new ways

00:40:21.110 --> 00:40:25.910
we are helping 1 billion people
make more sustainable choices.

00:40:25.910 --> 00:40:27.710
When it comes to
enterprises, one

00:40:27.710 --> 00:40:30.050
of the most important
sustainability choices

00:40:30.050 --> 00:40:32.780
is where to run your technology.

00:40:32.780 --> 00:40:37.190
IDC predicts cloud migrations
over the next four years

00:40:37.190 --> 00:40:41.690
could reduce carbon emissions
by over 1 billion metric tons

00:40:41.690 --> 00:40:45.140
or the equivalent of
removing 200 million cars

00:40:45.140 --> 00:40:47.710
off the road for a year.

00:40:47.710 --> 00:40:50.610
We are proud that Google
Cloud is the cleanest cloud

00:40:50.610 --> 00:40:52.310
in the industry.

00:40:52.310 --> 00:40:55.550
Earlier this year, we
introduced a way for customers

00:40:55.550 --> 00:40:59.660
to choose the cleanest regions
to run their workloads.

00:40:59.660 --> 00:41:01.970
Today, we are
expanding our portfolio

00:41:01.970 --> 00:41:05.600
of solutions and partnerships
to help reduce your carbon

00:41:05.600 --> 00:41:06.890
footprint.

00:41:06.890 --> 00:41:10.280
First, we have focused on
giving you greater transparency

00:41:10.280 --> 00:41:12.350
around carbon emissions data.

00:41:12.350 --> 00:41:15.740
We are announcing Carbon
Footprint, a new service

00:41:15.740 --> 00:41:19.100
to measure, track, and
report the gross carbon

00:41:19.100 --> 00:41:22.670
emissions associated with
your Google Cloud usage.

00:41:22.670 --> 00:41:26.520
Having this data at your
fingertips is really important.

00:41:26.520 --> 00:41:29.900
And we know that many customers
track sustainability data

00:41:29.900 --> 00:41:31.830
in other places.

00:41:31.830 --> 00:41:35.120
That's why I'm happy to announce
that Google Cloud Emission

00:41:35.120 --> 00:41:39.680
Data will integrate directly
into Salesforce Sustainability

00:41:39.680 --> 00:41:40.920
Cloud.

00:41:40.920 --> 00:41:44.470
We also want to give you the
tools to act on the data.

00:41:44.470 --> 00:41:47.310
So today, we are
introducing a new tool

00:41:47.310 --> 00:41:50.130
that will alert you when
you have idle workloads

00:41:50.130 --> 00:41:53.850
and make recommendations
to reduce carbon emissions.

00:41:53.850 --> 00:41:55.740
It's all part of
our goal to help

00:41:55.740 --> 00:41:59.430
make your Cloud transformation
secure and sustainable

00:41:59.430 --> 00:42:01.750
and solve for what's next.

00:42:01.750 --> 00:42:04.320
So on behalf of
Thomas and myself,

00:42:04.320 --> 00:42:06.840
let me thank you once
again for trusting

00:42:06.840 --> 00:42:10.360
us to be a partner with
you on this journey.

00:42:10.360 --> 00:42:13.830
And we hope you enjoy
the next three days.

00:42:13.830 --> 00:42:15.150
Thank you.

00:42:15.150 --> 00:42:17.300
[MUSIC PLAYING]

